# @hub-lanes

# lane-snapshot-publish (BH-6128, BH-6047 part 5 of 5): for each project, apply
# the write-backs Fly lane machines posted, then publish the project's
# blocked-resolver snapshot through the jobs worker when the lane is placed
# fly (bin/lib/lane-run-inputs.sh). 2,12,...: two minutes before the
# resolver's dispatch at 4,14,... Lease (BH-1000): a box that does not hold it
# runs nothing. Off: flags/lane-off-lane-snapshot-publish.
2,12,22,32,42,52 * * * * /root/harness/bin/hub-lease.sh check && /root/harness/bin/lane-snapshot-publish.sh >> /root/harness/logs/lane-snapshot-publish-cron.log 2>&1

# The same publisher for the pipeline-health project runs (BH-7252 C1): it
# applies their write-backs always, and publishes their snapshots once
# lane_placement.pipeline-health is fly. 8,18,...: two minutes before the
# pipeline-health dispatch at 0,10,... One line per moved lane, in this file:
# a fragment is named by its registry id, and the lane is lane-snapshot-publish.
8,18,28,38,48,58 * * * * /root/harness/bin/hub-lease.sh check && /root/harness/bin/lane-snapshot-publish.sh --lane pipeline-health >> /root/harness/logs/lane-snapshot-publish-cron.log 2>&1
